  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to data, with a lead from Sarah Tan. The project kicked off on June 15th with an initial phase one budget of $500,000, which was later approved for a total of $2M covering research, development, and marketing. Key milestones include the addition of team members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, as well as the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. The project has achieved breakthroughs in predictive analytics and AI algorithms, promising a 20% efficiency increase. Current phases involve moving from design to development under lead developer Omar Jensen, with upcoming updates and detailed reports scheduled for meetings in August, September, October, and November."
